# SPAM MAIL DETECTOR

## Machine Learning Based Email Classification System

---

## 1. ABSTRACT

Spam emails are unwanted messages that are frequently sent to users in large numbers. They may contain advertisements, fraudulent links, misleading information, or potentially harmful content. Manually identifying spam emails is time-consuming and unreliable. The **Spam Mail Detector** is a machine learning-based system developed to automatically classify emails as **Spam** or **Not Spam (Ham)**.

The system uses **Natural Language Processing (NLP)** techniques to preprocess email text and **TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency)** to convert text into numerical features. These features are then provided to a machine learning classification algorithm to predict the category of an email. The project demonstrates how machine learning can be applied to text classification and email filtering.

---

## 2. INTRODUCTION

Email has become an important communication medium for personal, educational, and professional purposes. However, the increasing use of email has also resulted in a large amount of unwanted spam messages.

Spam emails can waste users' time and may sometimes contain phishing links, fraudulent offers, or malicious content. Therefore, an automated spam detection system is useful for filtering unwanted messages.

The proposed Spam Mail Detector analyzes the content of an email and determines whether it is spam or legitimate. It uses Python, NLP, TF-IDF, and machine learning techniques to perform classification.

