## 5. LITERATURE REVIEW

Spam detection has traditionally relied on manually created rules and keyword-based filtering. However, such methods may fail when spammers change the wording or structure of their messages.

Machine learning provides a more flexible approach by learning patterns from previously classified emails. Different algorithms such as **Naive Bayes, Logistic Regression, Support Vector Machines, and Decision Trees** have been used for text classification.

Natural Language Processing further improves spam detection by allowing the system to process and analyze human language. In this project, TF-IDF is used to represent important words in email messages as numerical values.

